     5	
     6	In this section we show that for each solution $\vec{s}$ of $A\vec{x}=\vec{b}$ 
     7	there is always a path-like graph representation in ${\mathcal G}[A\vec{x}=\vec{b}]$.
     8	More precisely, we show that for any solution of an ILP instance with $n$ variables, there is a graph representation of this solution of path-width $2n$. Thus, the decidability of the ILP feasibility problem  can be directly derived by the decidability of FO on the class of bounded path-width graphs.  
